PORT=3000
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://fakeuser:fakepassword@localhost:5432/fakedb
BETTER_AUTH_SECRETS=1:replace-with-a-generated-secret-min-32-chars
BETTER_AUTH_URL=https://replace-with-origin
# Mandatory in production: comma-separated list of the PROXY HOPS between
# Tailscale and this container, so multi-hop X-Forwarded-For resolves to the
# real client IP (rate limiting per client, not global). Boot refuses to start
# in production without it. Direct dev/test runs (localhost, no proxy) may
# omit it.
#
# WARNING (gate review 2026-09-20, WR-03): this must NOT contain the range the
# clients themselves live in. 100.64.0.0/10 is the Tailscale CGNAT range — it
# is where every laptop, phone and mini has its tailnet address, NOT where the
# proxies are. Trusting it makes better-auth skip each client's own hop while
# walking X-Forwarded-For from the right, so every client collapses into one
# shared rate-limit bucket and a single attacker locks everyone out. The boot
# check rejects such a value.
#
# Determine the real value once per environment with `tests/live/xff-probe.md`
# and enter exactly the hop(s) the proxy chain appends — nothing else. For the
# Studio setup (tailscaled -> Traefik webapp entrypoint -> container) that is
# the coolify bridge gateway, and Traefik must be told to trust it first
# (`--entrypoints.webapp.forwardedHeaders.trustedIPs`), or the client IP never
# arrives at all:
# BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_PROXIES=192.0.2.1/32
# Runtime role URL for the server; owner/migration URL goes to
# MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL (see README).
# NODE_ENV: leer lassen / nicht setzen fuer produktionsaehnliche Laeufe.
# Die Boot-Haertung (Google-Credentials + BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_PROXIES Pflicht,
# TEST_OIDC_ISSUER verboten) greift bei JEDEM Wert ausser "development" und
# "test" — auch bei ungesetztem NODE_ENV. Deshalb steht hier bewusst KEIN
# NODE_ENV=development: ein in eine echte .env kopierter Dev-Wert wuerde die
# Haertung abschalten. Lokale Laeufe setzen es ueber die dev-Skripte
# (npm run dev:server / dev:client) selbst.
